{
  "id": "ui-footer-columns",
  "title": "Site footer: the three link columns are one component over a data array, not three hand-written subtrees",
  "description": "The corrected version of a footer that shipped wrong, so lift the fix and not the artefact. The reference build wrote Shop, Company and Help as three structurally identical Group(Text x5) subtrees: 27 nodes, one `repeated-sibling-subtree` warning, and a fourth column costs another six nodes. Here the whole nav is one Static Array of {title, links} driving a For Each over a FooterColumn, and the link list inside each column is a second For Each — repetition is data at BOTH levels, so 17 nodes total and a fourth column is one line of JSON and no nodes at all. ⚠️ Every object in an inline array carries an `id`. A plain array reaching a Repeater's Items is wrapped with Model.create, which mints a fresh anonymous id per element, so a second delivery of the same array matches nothing in the id diff and the list renders TWICE — measured at 31 texts where 19 were authored, forward then reversed. Ids make the diff idempotent. The row is a Columns node with layoutString \"1.6 1 1 1\" and smallLayout \"1\" below 760px, because no Group in the runtime has a breakpoint — the original crammed four tracks into 390px and broke words mid-syllable. Two more that are easy to miss: marginY is what gives the collapsed stack its vertical rhythm, and the legal row's two Texts need sizeMode contentSize, or they are each width 100%, justifyContent has nothing to distribute and flexWrap has nothing to wrap.",
  "demonstrates": [
    "net.noodl.visual.columns",
    "For Each",
    "Static Data",
    "Component Inputs",
    "Group",
    "Text"
  ],
  "components": [
